+# Proof outline
+
+The target is the exact Huang–Shi theorem 1.2 statement from the pinned
+Margulis module.  For a finite field F whose characteristic is 3, 5, 7, or
+11, it asserts the existence of a point in the quotient of SL₄(F((X))) by the
+image of SL₄(F[X]) such that the diagonal orbit has compact closure but is not
+closed.
+
+The local Lean work has four completed layers:
+
+1. Replay the polynomial-to-Laurent embedding and diagonal-subgroup
+   definitions used by the source.
+2. Freeze the quotient/orbit proposition and provide bidirectional
+   definitional transports between FrozenStatement and Target.
+3. Check the quotient carrier and the conditional characteristic
+   specialization at trust level zero.
+4. Audit all local declarations and exclude the upstream sorryAx body.
+
+The unresolved layer is the actual Huang–Shi construction and dynamics
+argument.  It must construct the quotient point and prove both halves of the
+orbit event.  No local elementary diagnostic supplies that layer.  The typed
+DAG in proof-units.json and the eight fragments in full-study.md isolate this
+cut precisely, so the handoff is readable but not machine-complete.
