+# Full study: Margulis.huang_shi_theorem_1_2
+
+## Scope and conclusion
+
+The pinned source is Huang–Shi theorem 1.2 in
+FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2504.17644/Margulis.lean, lines 73–90, revision
+2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669.  It asks for a point in the
+quotient of SL₄ over Laurent series by the polynomial lattice whose diagonal
+orbit is not closed although its closure is compact.  The provider theorem is
+sorryAx-dependent.  This package therefore freezes and audits the exact
+proposition but does not treat the provider body as proof evidence.
+
+The mathematical root is still open in the local Lean package.  The readable
+reconstruction below is complete for that nonacceptance boundary: every typed
+proof-DAG node has a unique content-addressed fragment, and the open cut is
+stated rather than replaced by an assumption.
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:BEGIN -->
+### PU-00 — exact frozen statement
+
+Hypotheses: a type F in universe u, instances Field F and Fintype F, and a
+proof that ringChar F belongs to the finite set {3, 5, 7, 11}.
+
+Inference: Statement.lean freezes the exact quotient and orbit event as
+OrbitConclusion F, universally quantifies the characteristic proof in
+FrozenStatement F, and makes Target F definitionally identical.  The forward
+and reverse transports are the identity.
+
+Output: the exact source proposition, without importing its proof body.
+
+Downstream: PU-01 and PU-03.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-00:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:BEGIN -->
+### PU-01 — source-definition replay
+
+Hypotheses: the pinned Mathlib algebra, matrix-group, Laurent-series, topology,
+and group-action interfaces.
+
+Inference: polyToLaurent is replayed as the source composition from
+polynomials through power series to Hahn/Laurent series.  The
+GeneralLinearGroup diagonal homomorphism, its range subgroup, and the
+SpecialLinearGroup comap subgroup are replayed from the source extension.
+The subgroup action is the restriction of the ambient special-linear action
+on the quotient.
+
+Output: every symbol in the frozen event elaborates without importing
+FormalConjecturesUtil or the sorryAx-bearing theorem.
+
+Downstream: PU-02 and PU-03.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-01:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:BEGIN -->
+### PU-02 — quotient carrier diagnostic
+
+Hypotheses: Field F and Fintype F.
+
+Inference: quotient_representative_nonempty selects the identity coset through
+QuotientGroup.mk.  This checks that the polynomial-to-Laurent range has the
+required subgroup type and that the homogeneous quotient is inhabited.
+
+Output: a kernel-checked Nonempty witness for the quotient carrier.  This does
+not imply either orbit property.
+
+Downstream: PU-06.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-02:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:BEGIN -->
+### PU-03 — characteristic specialization
+
+Hypotheses: an assumed FrozenStatement F or Target F and the exact membership
+proof ringChar F ∈ {3, 5, 7, 11}.
+
+Inference: characteristic_specialization applies the universally quantified
+statement to that membership proof.  The target-facing variant first uses the
+reverse definitional transport.
+
+Output: OrbitConclusion F conditionally on the full target theorem.  No
+existential witness is fabricated.
+
+Downstream: PU-04 and PU-06.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-03:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:BEGIN -->
+### PU-04 — unresolved Huang–Shi orbit construction
+
+Hypotheses: a finite field F of one of the four listed characteristics.
+
+Inference: the missing unit must formalize the Huang–Shi construction in the
+function-field homogeneous space, produce the quotient point z, prove
+compactness of the closure of its diagonal orbit, and prove that the orbit
+itself is not closed.  None of the local diagnostics entails these dynamical
+claims, and the source theorem cannot be used because its body depends on
+sorryAx.
+
+Output: unavailable.  Closing this unit would supply FrozenStatement F and
+therefore the exact machine root.
+
+Downstream: PU-05 and PU-06.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-04:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:BEGIN -->
+### PU-05 — trust boundary
+
+Hypotheses: none beyond the compiled local modules and pinned dependencies.
+
+Inference: Audit.lean probes the exact declarations and prints the axioms of
+every local theorem-level diagnostic.  The observed transitive foundation set
+is Classical.choice, Quot.sound, and propext.  Static scans reject sorry,
+admit, axiom, opaque, unsafe, and implemented_by declaration forms in the
+claim-owned Lean files.
+
+Output: the provider sorryAx is excluded, no claim-specific axiom or bodyless
+oracle is present, and the missing mathematical root remains explicit.
+
+Downstream: PU-06.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-05:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:BEGIN -->
+### PU-06 — root composition boundary
+
+Hypotheses: PU-00 through PU-05.
+
+Inference: the exact root could be composed from the frozen statement and
+definition replay, the characteristic branch, a genuine proof of PU-04, and
+the trust audit.  PU-02 is a carrier sanity check and is not evidence for the
+orbit event.  Because PU-04 is open, composition stops here.
+
+Output: no exact theorem declaration is produced.
+
+Downstream: PU-ROOT-OPEN.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-06:END -->
+
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:BEGIN -->
+### PU-ROOT-OPEN — provisional nonacceptance handoff
+
+Hypotheses: the audited DAG rooted at PU-06.
+
+Inference: retain the open mathematical cut, keep machine_complete false, keep
+readable_complete true for this frontier reconstruction, and require an
+independent canonical Master review.
+
+Output: a self-tested provisional handoff.  theorem_complete remains false
+because it is the conjunction of machine and readability completion, and the
+machine axis is open.
+
+Downstream: none.
+<!-- ANCHOR:PU-ROOT-OPEN:END -->
+
+## Reconstruction summary
+
+The forward map from eight required nodes to eight anchors is total and
+injective.  The reverse map has no unused anchor.  Each fragment states its
+hypotheses, inference, output, and downstream consumers.  This makes the
+package readable without overstating mathematical closure.
